---
import '../../styles/diagram.css';
---

<figure class="diagram">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 720 326" role="img" aria-labelledby="xc-title xc-desc">
    <title id="xc-title">Trade flow and identity across AWS and GCP</title>
    <desc id="xc-desc">
      A workload on EKS reaches Amazon MSK inside AWS using IRSA, and reaches the client’s
      GCP Pub/Sub topic using Workload Identity Federation, shown as the accented path
      crossing the cloud boundary. No static credentials are held on either side, and both
      ends generate from one Protobuf schema.
    </desc>

    <!-- Cloud boundaries -->
    <path
      class="diagram__art"
      stroke-dasharray="3 6"
      d="M16 40 L404 41 L403 246 L17 245 Z"></path>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="28" y="62">AWS — our account</text>

    <path
      class="diagram__art"
      stroke-dasharray="3 6"
      d="M452 41 L704 40 L703 245 L451 246 Z"></path>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="464" y="62">GCP — the client’s</text>

    <!-- EKS workload -->
    <path class="diagram__fill" d="M44 96 L193 97 L194 165 L45 164 Z"></path>
    <path class="diagram__art" d="M44 96 L193 97 L194 165 L45 164 Z"></path>
    <text class="diagram__label" x="62" y="125">EKS workload</text>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="62" y="145">service account</text>

    <!-- MSK -->
    <path class="diagram__art" d="M256 97 L375 96 L376 164 L255 165 Z"></path>
    <text class="diagram__label" x="274" y="125">MSK</text>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="274" y="145">Kafka</text>

    <!-- Pub/Sub -->
    <path class="diagram__art" d="M492 96 L661 97 L662 165 L491 164 Z"></path>
    <text class="diagram__label" x="510" y="125">Pub/Sub</text>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="510" y="145">the client’s topic</text>

    <!-- In-account path: IRSA -->
    <path class="diagram__art" d="M194 130 C 218 129, 236 131, 249 130"></path>
    <path class="diagram__ink-fill" d="M256 130 L246 125 L246 135 Z"></path>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="196" y="118">IRSA</text>

    <!-- Cross-cloud path: Workload Identity Federation. The one accent stroke. -->
    <path
      class="diagram__accent"
      d="M118 165 C 119 196, 117 210, 160 211 L540 211 C 576 210, 576 196, 576 172"></path>
    <path class="diagram__accent-fill" d="M576 165 L571 177 L581 177 Z"></path>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="168" y="232" style="fill: var(--accent)">
      Workload Identity Federation
    </text>

    <!-- The contract -->
    <path class="diagram__art" d="M16 280 L704 280" stroke-dasharray="3 6"></path>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="16" y="299">
      Protobuf schema in version control. Both ends generate from it, so a
    </text>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="16" y="313">
      field cannot change meaning without showing up as a diff.
    </text>
  </svg>

  <figcaption class="diagram__caption">
    Each hop uses the platform’s own federation rather than a key somebody has to rotate.
    The pod’s existing Kubernetes service account token is what GCP accepts, which is why
    neither side ends up holding a credential for the other.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
